<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div><div aria-labelledby="hero-heading"><div><h2 id="hero-heading"><img src="data:image/svg+xml;base64," width="300" height="53" alt="Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5"></h2><p>The everything computer. <span>Optimised.</span></p><p>With 2–3× the speed of the previous generation, and featuring silicon designed in‑house for the best possible performance, we’ve redefined the Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;experience.</p></div><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/50e89/raspberry-pi-5.webp 379w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/15759/raspberry-pi-5.webp 758w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/e8238/raspberry-pi-5.webp 1515w" sizes="(min-width: 1515px) 1515px, 100vw"><img data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 1515px) 1515px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="eager" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/e58b5/raspberry-pi-5.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/0f4e8/raspberry-pi-5.png 379w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/51d6d/raspberry-pi-5.png 758w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/c671804c05a51efc4e3c2a1bdcbafbcf/e58b5/raspberry-pi-5.png 1515w" alt=""></picture></div></div><div aria-labelledby="pi-16gb-heading"><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/f6ea0/16gb.webp 100w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/3ee75/16gb.webp 200w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/f7ad0/16gb.webp 400w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/33b96/16gb.webp 800w" sizes="(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw"><img data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 400px) 400px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="eager" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/b0461/16gb.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/4e4d4/16gb.png 100w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/4698f/16gb.png 200w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/b0461/16gb.png 400w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/8f6eca535dbb23a21eb41a748050e3a0/3fd03/16gb.png 800w" alt=""></picture></div><div><h2 id="pi-16gb-heading"><img src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/16gb-wordmark-mobile-1e30e607a7fdbe9d3987a9fa98023cf7.svg" width="300" height="111" alt="Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5 16GB"><img src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/16gb-wordmark-ba563b95afec288061b5307543fc1b21.svg" width="435" height="42" alt="Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5 16GB"></h2><p>For power users and professional&nbsp;applications.</p><p>Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5 16GB is available now for <strong>$305</strong>.</p></div></div><div><section aria-labelledby="rp1-heading"><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 1400px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/d8098/rp1.webp 350w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/c73ff/rp1.webp 700w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/83b0f/rp1.webp 1400w"><img data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 1400px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/6ebc2/rp1.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/c2b9a/rp1.png 350w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/89684/rp1.png 700w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/30b0a05490a436a282259a767caba3fb/6ebc2/rp1.png 1400w"></picture></div><div><h2 id="rp1-heading">RP1</h2><p>Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5 is built using the RP1 I/O controller, a package containing silicon designed in-house at Raspberry&nbsp;Pi.</p><p>USB 3 has more total bandwidth, for much faster transfer speeds.</p><p>Camera and DSI display connectors are interchangeable, so you can have one of each, or two the same.</p></div></section><section aria-labelledby="soc-heading"><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 1400px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/d8098/soc.webp 350w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/c73ff/soc.webp 700w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/83b0f/soc.webp 1400w"><img data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 1400px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/6ebc2/soc.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/c2b9a/soc.png 350w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/89684/soc.png 700w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/76ec39ad312906148a43b0e5e1ab0e36/6ebc2/soc.png 1400w"></picture></div><div><h2 id="soc-heading">More than twice as fast and infinitely smoother</h2><p>Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5 features the Broadcom BCM2712 quad-core Arm Cortex A76 processor @ 2.4GHz, making it up to three times faster than the previous generation. With RAM variants up to 16GB, this is the fastest, smoothest Raspberry&nbsp;Pi experience yet.</p></div></section><section aria-labelledby="pci-express-heading"><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 1400px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/d8098/pci-express.webp 350w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/c73ff/pci-express.webp 700w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/83b0f/pci-express.webp 1400w"><img data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 1400px) 1400px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/6ebc2/pci-express.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/c2b9a/pci-express.png 350w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/89684/pci-express.png 700w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/6fa72be44172792c5541c84c9ef467ef/6ebc2/pci-express.png 1400w"></picture></div><div><h2 id="pci-express-heading">All aboard the PCI express</h2><p>This addition to Raspberry&nbsp;Pi allows you to connect an M.2 SSD to your Raspberry&nbsp;Pi, giving you speedy data transfer and super-fast boot.</p></div></section></div><div aria-labelledby="os-heading"><header><p>The latest release of Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;OS is made to get the most from Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5. The newest version of our operating system delivers a superb desktop performance, making it an ideal computer for work, leisure, enterprise, and more.</p></header><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 2280px) 2280px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/56e5b/raspberry-pi-os.webp 570w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/7d20f/raspberry-pi-os.webp 1140w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/00562/raspberry-pi-os.webp 2280w"><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 2280px) 2280px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/3b00d/raspberry-pi-os.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/e2ae8/raspberry-pi-os.png 570w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/bb546/raspberry-pi-os.png 1140w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/45eb3aa28d8f3d57842e8cd5e80c2969/3b00d/raspberry-pi-os.png 2280w"></picture></div></div><div aria-labelledby="not-all-heading"><header><h2 id="not-all-heading">That’s not all</h2></header><div><div><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/c65bc/power-button.webp 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/214a8/power-button.webp 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/2b014/power-button.webp 601w"><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/08f46/power-button.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/de3a1/power-button.png 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/26025/power-button.png 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/5c143958efa9828ec0b20164d2bc9f29/08f46/power-button.png 601w"></picture></div><p>Power button</p></div><div><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/c65bc/dual-4k.webp 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/214a8/dual-4k.webp 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/2b014/dual-4k.webp 601w"><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/08f46/dual-4k.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/de3a1/dual-4k.png 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/26025/dual-4k.png 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/d4e27b61631cbb2caec9c56e3d090a61/08f46/dual-4k.png 601w"></picture></div><p>Dual 4Kp60</p></div><div><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/c65bc/rtc.webp 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/214a8/rtc.webp 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/2b014/rtc.webp 601w"><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/08f46/rtc.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/de3a1/rtc.png 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/26025/rtc.png 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/044f174a1b537d49be0d88f7c7d70c63/08f46/rtc.png 601w"></picture></div><p>Real-time clock</p></div><div><div data-gatsby-image-wrapper=""><picture><source type="image/webp" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/c65bc/uart.webp 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/214a8/uart.webp 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/2b014/uart.webp 601w"><img data-gatsby-image-ssr="" data-main-image="" sizes="(min-width: 601px) 601px, 100vw" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="" src="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/08f46/uart.png" srcset="https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/de3a1/uart.png 150w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/26025/uart.png 301w,https://assets.raspberrypi.com/static/aa747872320377d3d51f4f0b5206581d/08f46/uart.png 601w"></picture></div><p>UART debug port</p></div></div></div><div aria-labelledby="accessories-heading"><header><h2 id="accessories-heading">Accessories</h2><p>Our official accessories for Raspberry&nbsp;Pi&nbsp;5 are specially designed to help you get the best possible performance from your computer.</p></header></div><div aria-label="Specification" id="specs"><h2 id="specification">Specification</h2><div><p>Broadcom BCM2712 2.4GHz quad-core 64-bit Arm Cortex-A76 CPU, with cryptography extensions, 512KB per-core L2 caches and a 2MB shared L3 cache</p><p>VideoCore VII GPU, supporting OpenGL ES 3.1, Vulkan 1.3</p><p>Dual 4Kp60 HDMI® display output with HDR support</p><p>4Kp60 HEVC decoder</p><p>LPDDR4X-4267 SDRAM (1GB, 2GB, 4GB, 8GB, and 16GB)</p><p>Dual-band 802.11ac Wi-Fi®</p><p>Bluetooth 5.0 / Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE)</p><p>microSD card slot, with support for high-speed SDR104 mode</p><p>2 × USB 3.0 ports, supporting simultaneous 5Gbps operation</p><p>2 × USB 2.0 ports</p><p>Gigabit Ethernet, with PoE+ support (requires separate PoE+ HAT)</p><p>2 × 4-lane MIPI camera/display transceivers</p><p>PCIe 2.0 x1 interface for fast peripherals (requires separate M.2 HAT or other adapter)</p><p>5V/5A DC power via USB-C, with Power Delivery support</p><p>Raspberry Pi standard 40-pin header</p><p>Real-time clock (RTC), powered from external battery</p><p>Power button<br></p></div><h2 id="your-questions-answered">Your questions answered</h2><div><h3>Will older versions of Raspberry Pi OS work with Raspberry Pi 5?</h3><p>The current version of Raspberry Pi OS, <a href="https://www.raspberrypi.com/news/trixie-the-new-version-of-raspberry-pi-os/" rel="noreferrer">Trixie</a>, and the legacy version, Bookworm, work with Raspberry Pi 5. Versions older than Bookworm do not.</p><h3>Will my Raspberry Pi 4 power supply work with Raspberry Pi 5?</h3><p>Raspberry Pi 5 is a higher-performance computer than Raspberry Pi 4, and you may have problems using an under-powered supply. We recommend a high-quality 5V 5A USB-C  power supply, such as the new Raspberry Pi 27W USB-C Power Supply.</p><h3>Will my Raspberry Pi 5 fit my Raspberry Pi 4 case?</h3><p>Raspberry Pi 5 won't fit the Raspberry Pi 4 Case. We recommend the Raspberry Pi Case for Raspberry Pi 5, designed to help you get the most out of our newest computer.</p><h3>Does Raspberry Pi 5 need active cooling?</h3><p>Raspberry Pi 5 is faster and more powerful than prior-generation Raspberry Pis, and like most general-purpose computers, it will perform best with active cooling. The Raspberry Pi Case for Raspberry Pi 5, with its integrated fan, is one way to provide this.</p></div><h2>Documents</h2><div><ul><li><a href="https://pip.raspberrypi.com/documents/RP-008348-DS-raspberry-pi-5-product-brief.pdf">Raspberry Pi 5 product brief</a></li><li><a href="https://pip.raspberrypi.com/documents/RP-008347-DS-1-raspberry-pi-5-mechanical-drawing.pdf">Raspberry Pi 5 mechanical drawing</a></li><li><a href="https://www.raspberrypi.com/documentation/computers/raspberry-pi.html">Getting started documentation</a></li><li><a href="https://pip.raspberrypi.com/documents/RP-008370-DS-1-rp1-peripherals.pdf">RP1 peripherals documentation</a></li></ul></div><h2 id="compliance">Compliance</h2><div><p>Raspberry Pi 5 has undergone extensive compliance testing and meets a number of regional and international standards.</p><div><p>View and download&nbsp;<strong><a href="https://pip.raspberrypi.com/" rel="noreferrer">relevant certificates and conformity documents</a>.</strong><br>If you require any further information regarding compliance, please contact us at&nbsp;<strong><a href="mailto:compliance@raspberrypi.com" rel="noreferrer">compliance@raspberrypi.com</a>.</strong></p><p>The Adopted Trademarks HDMI®, HDMI High-Definition Multimedia Interface, and the HDMI Logo are trademarks or registered trademarks of HDMI Licensing Administrator, Inc. in the United States and other countries.</p></div><p><img src="https://rpf-products.cdn.prismic.io/rpf-products/da91d806-2be4-4c24-ac38-38f6a4ec4465__HDMI%2520logo.svg?auto=compress,format" alt="HDMI logo"></p></div><h2>Obsolescence</h2><div><p>Raspberry Pi 5</p><p> will remain in production until at least </p><p>January 2036</p></div></div></div></div>